hadiths[150]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5401","4508 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Abu Jubayrah, from elders of the Ansar (may Allah be pleased with them), that they heard him, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: I was sent in the breath of the Hour. Sufyan said: meaning the breathing of the Hour."
"5402","4509 - Abu Bakr said: Waki' narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Shibl ibn Awf, from Abu Jubayrah, from some elders of the Ansar (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent and the Hour is like these two, and I preceded it in the breath of the Hour."
"5403","4510/1 - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us: Harun ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu al-Jallas, who said: I heard Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) say to Abdullah ibn Saba' al-Saba'i: Woe to you! By Allah, nothing was confided to me that was hidden from anyone of the people; by Allah, I heard him say: Before the Hour there will be thirty liars, and you are one of them."
"5404","4510/2 - Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us, with this same report."
"5405","4510/3 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, with it."
"5406","4511 - Al-Harith said: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us: my father Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until seventy liars come forth before the Hour."
"5407","4512 - Abu Ya'la said: Zuhayr told us: Jarir told us, from Layth, from Bishr, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the emergence of the Dajjal there will be more than seventy dajjals."
"5408","Chapter 42: Mention of Ibn Sayyad and uncertainty whether he is the Dajjal. 4513 - Ishaq said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, who said: I met Ibn Sayyad one day, with him a Jewish man; his eye had gone out, though it had been protruding like a camel's eye. When I saw it I said: Ibn Sayyad! I adjure you by Allah, when did your eye go out? He wiped it and said: I do not know, by the Merciful. I said: you lie; you do not know, though it is in your head? The Jew claimed to me that I struck my hand on his chest, though I do not know that I did that. I said: be gone, you will not exceed your measure. He said: yes, I will not exceed my measure. He mentioned something I do not remember. He said: I mentioned that to Hafsah (may Allah be pleased with her), and she said: avoid this man, for we are told the Dajjal emerges at an anger he becomes angry with. I said: Muslim brought the hadith of Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), from Hafsah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Dajjal emerges at an anger he becomes angry with, but he did not bring the beginning of the story mentioned here with this wording."
"5409","4514 - Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: Ibn Sayyad's mother bore him with a caul, one-eyed, circumcised."
"5410","4515 - Al-Harith said: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us: Abbad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard of Ibn Sayyad, he went to him with some of his companions; his mother said: he is playing with the boys. She said: I bore him one-eyed, circumcised. He called for him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I believe in Allah and His messengers. He said: I have hidden something for you, what is it? He said: Dukhkh. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: be gone. He said: see what you see? He said: I see a whirlwind and a throne upon water. He said: he has been confounded. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: shall I kill him, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he is the Dajjal you will have no power to kill him, and if he is not the Dajjal it is not lawful to kill him."
"5411","4516 - Abu Bakr said: Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, who said: Uqbah ibn Amr said to Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with them both): will you not tell us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: yes; I heard him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: With the Dajjal when he emerges there will be water and fire; as for what people see as water, it is burning fire, and as for what people see as fire, it is cool water. Whoever of you reaches that, let him fall into what he sees as fire, for it is cool water. Uqbah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: and I heard him say that. I said: the hadith of Hudhayfah is with them."
"5412","4517/1 - Abu Ya'la said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Dajjal there will be deceitful years in which rain increases and crops decrease; the truthful will be disbelieved and the liar believed; the treacherous trusted and the trustworthy distrusted; and the Ruwaybidah will speak in them. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the Ruwaybidah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: one of no account."
"5413","4517/2 - Al-Bazzar narrated it: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, with it; and in its chain he said, from Ibn Ishaq: Ibrahim narrated to me; and at its end he said: And what is the Ruwaybidah? He said: the worthless man who speaks about public affairs."
"5414","4518 - Musaddad said: Yahya, that is al-Qattan, narrated to me, from Wa'il ibn Dawud: Abdullah ibn Subayh, or Subayh, freedman of Banu Layth, narrated to me, saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) say: When the Dajjal emerges he will emerge from toward the east; his troops and outposts will be many, and none will reach him except one who says: I am a delegate. A man will come saying: I am a delegate. When the Dajjal sees him he will say: son of Adam, do you not know I am your lord? He will say: no; you are Allah's enemy, the Dajjal. He will say: I shall kill you. He will say: even if you kill me. He said: he will take a saw and place it between his front teeth and split him in two; then he will say to those around him: what do you think, if I revive him? They will say: then we will be certain you are our lord. He said: he will revive him and say to him: son of Adam, you claimed I am not your lord. He will say: never was I more clear-sighted about you than now. He will say: I shall slaughter you. He will say: even if you slaughter me. He said: he will mean to slaughter him but cannot slaughter him; then one from beneath him will say: if you are truthful then slaughter me. At that his troops will doubt him, and the son of Mary (peace be upon him) will descend upon him; when he sees him and finds his breath he will melt as lead melts."
"5415","4519 - Musaddad said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from al-Uryan ibn al-Haytham, from his father, who said: I entered upon Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah and he mentioned a story; Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: Is there in your land a land called Kawtha, of salt marsh and palms? He said: yes. He said: The Dajjal will emerge from it."
"5416","4520 - Yahya narrated to us: Fitr narrated to us: Abu al-Tufayl narrated to me, saying: I heard from one of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hadith about the Dajjal; I never heard a weightier hadith from him: he will come on a donkey; a man will come in the image of one of his household and say: O so-and-so, I call you to the truth; my affair is true."
"5417","4521 - Musaddad also said: Abdullah ibn Dawud told us: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Ubayd ibn Umayr (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I warn you of the Dajjal, the hadith. Muhadir differed, saying: from Hisham, from Wahb, from Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both); Ibn Hibban brought it, and the first is more correct despite its being mursal."
"5418","4522 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Hisham ibn Sulayman al-Makhzumi narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Rafi' narrated to us, from one who told him, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), and he mentioned the hadith of the story of the Dajjal. It is with Ibn Majah by another way, from Isma'il ibn Rafi', from Yahya ibn Abi Amr, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him); and Hisham added in it: whoever of you meets him, let him spit in his face."
"5419","4523 - Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Husayn ibn Hasan ibn Atiyyah al-Awfi narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, saying: he asked Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) about the Dajjal, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet warned his people of the Dajjal; lo, he has eaten food; lo, I entrust to you about him a charge no prophet entrusted to his ummah: lo, his right eye is effaced as though it were spittle on the side of a wall; lo, his left eye is as though a brilliant star; with him the like of Paradise and Hell: the fire is a green meadow, and paradise dusty with smoke; before him two men warning the people of the towns; whenever they enter a town they warn its people; when they leave it, the first of the Dajjal's companions enters and enters all the towns except Makkah and Madinah, forbidden to him; the believers are scattered in the earth, and Allah the Exalted will gather them. A man of them will say: by Allah, I shall go and look at this one of whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) warned us. His companions will say to him: we will not let you come to him; had we known he would not tempt you we would have left your way, but we fear he will tempt you and you will follow him. He will refuse but to come to him; he will go until when he reaches the nearest outpost of his outposts they will seize him and ask him: what is his affair, and where does he mean? He will say: I mean the lying Dajjal. They will say: do you say that? They will write to him: we have seized a man saying so-and-so; shall we kill him or send him to you? He will say: send him to me. They will go with him to him; when he sees him he will recognize him by the description of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and say to him: you are the lying Dajjal of whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) warned us. The Dajjal will say to him: do you say that? You shall obey me in what I command you, or I shall split you in two. The believing servant will call out among the people: O people, this is the lying Messiah. He will order him stretched with his legs, then order an iron blade placed on the base of his spine and split him in two. Then the Dajjal will say to his allies: do you see, if I revive him for you, do you not know I am your lord? They will say: yes. He will take a staff and strike one of his halves, or the ground, and he will stand upright. When his allies see that they will believe him, love him, be certain he is their lord, and follow him. The Dajjal will say to the believing servant: will you not believe in me? He will say: I am now more clear-sighted about you than before. Then he will call among the people: O people, this is the lying Messiah; whoever obeys him is in the Fire, and whoever disobeys him is in Paradise. The Dajjal will say: you shall obey me or I shall slaughter you. He will say: by Allah, I shall never obey you; you are the liar. He will order him laid down and order his slaughter, but he will have no power over him; he is given power over him only once. He will take him by his hands and feet and cast him into the fire, which is without smoke. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: that man is the nearest of my ummah to me and the highest in rank. Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I said: how will he perish? He said: Allah knows best. I said: is it Jesus son of Mary (peace and prayer be upon him) who will destroy him? He said: Allah knows best, except that Allah the Exalted will destroy him and those with him. I said: what will be after him? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us: people will plant plantings after him and take wealth after him. I said: glory be to Allah, after the Dajjal? He said: yes. They will remain on earth as long as Allah wills them to remain; then Gog and Magog will be released and destroy all on earth except one who clings to a fortress. When they finish with the people of the earth some will turn to others and say: only those in fortresses and those in heaven remain; they will shoot their arrows, and they will fall back changed with blood. They will say: you are relieved of those in heaven; only those in fortresses remain. They will besiege them until siege and trial press hard upon them; while they are so, Allah the Exalted will send upon them worms in their necks that will break their necks, and they will fall dead upon one another. A man will say: the Lord of the Ka'bah has killed them. He said: they do this only in deceit; if we go out to them they will destroy us as they destroyed our brothers. He will say: open the gate for me. His companions will say: we will not open. He will say: let me down by a rope. When he descends he will find them dead, and people will come out of their fortresses. Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) told me that Allah the Exalted will make their cattle a life for them on which they graze, finding nothing else. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us: people will plant plantings after them and take wealth. He said: I said: glory be to Allah, after Gog and Magog? He said: yes. While they are in their trades, a caller will call from heaven: Allah's command has come. The people of the earth will panic when they hear the call, and turn to one another, then return to their trades, markets and crafts. While they are so they will be called again: O people, Allah's command has come. They will go toward the call they heard; a man will flee from his sheep and goods toward the call, meeting Allah, dazed about their cattle; then milch camels will be neglected. While they are so, hastening toward the call, they will meet Allah the Exalted in shades of clouds: And the Trumpet will be blown and all in the heavens and earth will swoon except whom Allah wills; they will remain as long as Allah wills; then it will be blown therein again, and behold they will stand looking; then Hell will come with sighing and roaring; then it will be called out, and he mentioned the hadith at length. The authors of the Sunan brought from it the story of intercession, the story of the sending of the Fire, and other than that; in this wording there is some variance, and what is in the Sahih is more correct; success is by Allah."
"5420","4524 - Abu Ya'la said: Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Dajjal has eaten and walked in the markets."
"5421","4525 - Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi said: Musa ibn Mutayr narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None is given power over the Dajjal except Jesus son of Mary (peace be upon him)."
"5422","4526/1 - Ishaq said: Jarir told us: al-Mughirah told us: al-Sha'bi told us, from Fatimah bint Qays, in the story of the Dajjal, she said: And he is among you, O ummah."
"5423","4526/2 - Mu'adh ibn Hisham told us: my father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah, in the story of Tamim al-Dari with the Dajjal; at its beginning: Tamim told me a hadith that gladdened me, and I wished to tell it to you that you may rejoice as your Prophet rejoiced with it."
"5424","4526/3 - And in it: Abu Usamah told us: al-Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah, with the hadith; and in it: Tamim came to me and told me news that kept me from the midday nap out of joy and delight."
"5425","4526/4 - And in it: al-Sha'bi said: I met al-Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah, and he said: my father narrated to me with it; and he added: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck with his hand toward the east nearly twenty times. 4526/5 - Abu Usamah told us, saying: one who heard al-Sha'bi told me; he added in it: that he asked them whether the people had built Thiqa? And in it that he struck his foot on the sole of his foot; and in it: that he said from the direction of Iraq."
"5426","Chapter 43: Gog and Magog. 4527 - al-Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Jabir, from Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), and he mentioned a raised hadith, saying: Then he began telling us: Gog and Magog are of the children of Adam; had they been sent upon people they would have spoiled their livelihoods; none of them dies but leaves of his offspring a thousand or more; and behind them three nations: Tawil, Taris and Mansak."
"5427","4528 - Abu Ya'la said: Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Gog and Magog dig every day."
"5428","4529 - Ghassan, that is Ibn al-Rabi', narrated to us: Musa narrated to us, from his father, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come upon a believer; Allah the Exalted will send a wind that will blow, and no believer will remain but will die."
"5429","4530 - Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Tariq, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), I think from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Hour will not come until Allah sends a red wind from Yemen, by which Allah the Mighty and Majestic will gather every soul believing in Allah and the Last Day; people will not notice it from the few who die in it: an old man died among so-and-so, an old woman died among so-and-so; the Book of Allah the Exalted will be taken away by night and raised to heaven, and no verse of it will remain on earth; the earth will cast out its burdens of gold and silver, and they will be of no use after that day; a man will pass by them and kick them with his foot and say: for this those before us killed, and today it is of no use."
"5430","Chapter 44: Trial of the grave and punishment of the grave. 4531 - Al-Harith said: Sa'd ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Ata' ibn Yasar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him): O Umar, how will you be when you die and they measure for you three cubits and a span in a cubit and a span, then return to you and wash you, shroud you and embalm you, then carry you until they place you in it, then heap dust over you? When they turn from you there will come to you the two triers of the grave, Munkar and Nakir, their voices like crashing thunder and their eyes like flashing lightning; they will shake you, rattle you and frighten you; how will you be then, O Umar? He said: O Messenger of Allah, and with me my mind? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: yes. He (may Allah be pleased with him) said: then I shall suffice you against them. Its men are trustworthy despite its being mursal."
"5431","4532 - Abu Ya'la said: Ibrahim al-Sami narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thumamah ibn Abdullah, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a boy, or a girl, and said: Had anyone been saved from the squeeze of the grave, this boy would have been saved. Its chain is sound."
"5432","4533 - Musaddad said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from al-Nu'man ibn Abi Ayyash, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The straitened living which Allah the Exalted mentions is the punishment of the grave."
"5433","4534 - He said: And Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abdullah al-Danaj narrated to us, saying: I witnessed Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) when a man said to him: O Abu Hamzah, some people deny intercession. He (may Allah be pleased with him) said: do not sit with them. Then a man said to him: some people deny the punishment of the grave. He (may Allah be pleased with him) said: do not sit with them."
"5434","4535 - Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Bahr narrated to us: Adi ibn Abi Umarah narrated to us: Ziyad al-Numayri narrated to us, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave; by the One in whose hand is my soul, I have seen how they are punished in their graves."
"5435","4536/1 - Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn Jammaz narrated to us, from Abu Dawud, who had met a dozen Companions, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) and others of the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The punishment of the grave is true; whoever does not believe in it will be punished."
"5436","4536/2 - Rawh narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from (lacuna)."
"5437","4537 - Abu Ya'la said: Abu al-Rabi', and he is not al-Zahrani, narrated to us: Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from al-Haytham ibn Malik al-Ta'i, from Abd al-Rahman ibn A'idh al-Azdi, from Abu al-Hajjaj al-Thumali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The grave says to the dead when he is placed in it: woe to you, O son of Adam! What deceived you about me? Did you not know I am the house of trial and the house of darkness? What deceived you about me when you used to pass by me strutting? If he was righteous, one answering on behalf of the grave will answer: have you seen, if he used to command good and forbid evil? Then the grave will say: then I return upon him green, and his soul ascends to the Lord of the worlds. Ibn A'idh said to him: O Abu al-Hajjaj, what is the strutter? He said: one who puts a foot forward and a foot back, like your walk sometimes, O son of my brother; and on that day he dresses and prepares."
"5438","4538 - Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us that Abu al-Samh told him, from Ibn Hujayrah, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The believer in his grave is in a garden; his grave is widened for him seventy cubits and lit for him like the moon on the night of full moon. Do you know concerning what this verse was sent down: Then he will have a straitened living, and We shall gather him on the Day of Resurrection blind? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: the punishment of the disbeliever in his grave; by the One in whose hand is my soul, ninety-nine dragons are set upon him. Do you know what the dragon is? He said: ninety-nine snakes, each snake with seven heads, blowing into his body, biting him and scratching him until the Day of Resurrection."
"5439","Chapter 45: Description of the resurrection. 4539 - Ishaq said: Jarir told us, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal ibn Amr: Qays ibn al-Sakan and Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) told Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) this hadith, saying: When people are gathered on the Day of Resurrection they will stand for forty, with the sun over their heads, their eyes staring toward the heaven, awaiting the decree, every righteous and wicked one of them, no human of them speaking. Then a caller will call: is it not justice from your Lord who created you, formed you and provided for you, then you worshipped other than Him, that He entrust each people to what they followed? They will say: yes. An angel will call that three times. Then there will appear to each people the gods they used to worship, and they will follow them until they bring them to the Fire. The believers and hypocrites will remain; the believers will fall prostrate, while the spines of the hypocrites will be fused into a single bone like the horns of cows, and they will fall on their backs. Allah the Exalted will say to them: raise your heads to your light according to your deeds. A man will raise his head with his light before him like a mountain; a man will raise his head with his light before him like a palace; a man will raise his head with his light before him like a house, until he mentioned the like of a tree. They will pass over the Path like lightning, like wind, like the gallop of a horse, and like a man's running, until the last of the people remains with his light on his big toe like a lamp, at times lighting for him and at times hidden from him; the Fire will snatch at him, and he will remain so until he comes out. He will say: none knows what was saved from it but I, and none was struck like what struck me; only its heat struck me and I was saved from it. He said: a gate in Paradise will be opened for him, and he will say: my Lord, let me enter this. He will say: My servant, perhaps if I let you enter you will ask Me for other than it. He said: he will let him enter, and while he marvels at what he is in, another gate will be opened for him, and what he is in will seem small in his eyes, and he will say: my Lord, let me enter this. He will say: did you not claim you would not ask Me for other than it? He will say: by Your might and majesty, if You let me enter it I shall not ask You for other than it. He said: he will let him enter until he lets him enter four gates, each of which he asks for. Then a man like light will meet him; when he sees him he will bow and prostrate to him. He will say: what is your affair? He will say: are you not my Lord? He will say: I am but a steward; for you in Paradise are a thousand stewards over a thousand palaces, between every two palaces a journey of a thousand years, the farthest seen as the nearest. Then a gate of green chrysolite will be opened for him, with seventy gates, in each gate wives, couches and cushions; he will sit with his wife, and she will hand him the cup and say: since you handed me the cup you are handsomer than before it by seventyfold; upon her seventy robes of various colors, the marrow of her leg seen; the man will wear his clothes upon her liver, and her liver is his mirror. This is a sound connected chain, its men trustworthy."
"5440","4540 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to me, from Shu'bah, from Salamah, from Abu al-Za'ra', from Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Trumpet is like the shape of a horn blown into. Sound, stopped."
"5441","4541 - Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Sahba' narrated to us: Abu Ghalib narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Ala' ibn Ziyad say to Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): how will people be raised on the Day of Resurrection? He (may Allah be pleased with him) said: they will be raised while the heaven drizzles upon them."
"5442","4542 - Abu Bakr said: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Abu Aqil Abdullah ibn Aqil al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Sinan al-Rahawi: Abu Yahya al-Kala'i told us, saying: I heard Abu Umamah al-Bahili (may Allah be pleased with him) say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I know the last man of my ummah to pass the Path: a man writhing on the Path like a boy when his father brings him near; his hand slips once and the Fire strikes it, his foot slips once and the Fire strikes it. He said: the angels will say to him: what if Allah the Exalted raised you in this station of yours and you walked straight, will you tell us of every deed you did? He said: he will say: yes, by His might, I shall hide nothing of my deeds. He said: they will say to him: stand and walk straight. He will stand and walk until he passes the Path. They will say to him: tell us of the deed you did. He will say to himself: if I tell them of what I did they will return me to my place. He said: he will say: no, by His might, I never committed a sin at all. He said: they will say to him: we have proof against you. He said: he will look right and left, does he see any of the humans who used to witness in this world; he will see no one, and will say: bring your proof. Then Allah the Exalted will seal his mouth, and his hands, feet and thigh will speak of his deed. He will say: yes, by Your might, I did them; I have grave destructive sins. He said: Allah the Exalted will say to him: go, I have forgiven them for you."
"5443","4543 - Abu Bakr also said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah: Muhammad ibn Ka'b narrated to us, from Awf ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I know the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise: a man who used to ask Allah the Exalted to move him away from the Fire, until when the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire the Fire, he is between that. He will say: my Lord! Bring me near the gate of Paradise. It will be said: O son of Adam, did you not ask to be moved away from the Fire? He will say: my Lord, and who is like You? Bring me near the gate of Paradise. He will be brought near it, and will see a tree at the gate of Paradise, and will say: my Lord, bring me near it that I may shade in its shade and eat of its fruit. He, glory and majesty be to Him, will say: O son of Adam! Did you not say? He will say: my Lord! And who is like You; bring me near it. He will see better than that and will say: my Lord, bring me near it. He, majestic in majesty, will say: O son of Adam, did you not say? He will say: my Lord, and who is like You? Bring me near. It will be said to him: run, and for you is what your feet reach and your eyes see. He said: he will run until when he tires, meaning is exhausted, he will say: my Lord, is this for me and this? He will say: for you the like of it and multiples. He will say: my Lord is pleased with me; had He let me clothe and feed the people of Paradise I would have enriched them."
"5444","4544 - Abu Ya'la said: Ya'qub al-Dawraqi narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Umayr al-Ansari, who said: We sat beside Ibn Umar and Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with them); one of them said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Sweat on the Day of Resurrection will reach up people. One of them said: to the earlobe; the other said: until sweat bridles him. Then Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: thus. Abu Asim described it, passing his finger from the earlobe to his mouth: this and that are the same. Al-Hakim narrated it by way of Abu Asim, saying in it: Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said, with his finger under the earlobe; and he said: sound in chain."
"5445","4545 - Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Husayn narrated to us: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Path is like the edge of a sword, slippery, a place of slipping, with thorns and hooks."
"5446","4546 - Musaddad said: Khalid narrated to us, from al-Hajari, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic will call a servant on the Day of Resurrection and remind him of His favors and blessings, until he will say among what he says: you asked Me on such-and-such a day to marry you to so-and-so, naming her, and you married her."
"5447","4547 - Abu Ya'la said: Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The disbeliever will be bridled by sweat on the Day of Resurrection, and will say: relieve me even to the Fire."
"5448","4548 - Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The disbeliever will be reckoned on the Day of Resurrection until sweat bridles him, until he will say: relieve me even to the Fire."
"5449","4549 - al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us: Mu'tamir narrated to us, from al-Fadl ibn Isa: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to me, saying: Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) told him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shame and disgrace will reach the son of Adam at the Resurrection before Allah the Mighty and Majestic such that a man will wish to be ordered to the Fire."
"5450","4550 - Al-Bazzar said: Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata' narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Isa narrated to us, from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sweat will cling to a man in the standing until he will say: my Lord! Your sending me to the Fire is easier for me than what I find, though he knows what severe punishment is in it. And he said: we know it only by this chain."
"5451","4551 - Abd said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us: my father narrated to us, saying: Abu Harun al-Ghitrif told him that Abu al-Sha'tha' told him that Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) told him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told him: that the Trustworthy Spirit (peace be upon him) told him: that Allah the Mighty and Majestic has decreed that a servant's deed be brought on the Day of Resurrection, his good and his evil, and some set off against some; if one good deed remains for him, Allah will widen Paradise for him as He wills. Ibrahim said: my father said: I said to Abu Salamah Yazdad: if the good deed is gone and nothing remains? He said: Those from whom We accept the best of what they did and overlook their evils, the verse."
"5452","4552 - Abd said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Ayyub ibn Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Of my ummah there will come on the Day of Resurrection like the flood, and the angels will say: with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came of his ummah more than came with all the prophets. Weak."
"5453","4553/1 - Abu Dawud said: Durust ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), raised: The sun and moon are two hamstrung bulls in the Fire."
"5454","4553/2 - Musaddad said: Durust narrated to us, with it."
"5455","4553/3 - Abu Ya'la said: Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us: Durust narrated to us, with it."
"5456","4554 - Abu Ya'la said: Ibn Muti' narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Kawthar ibn Hakim, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will be gathered barefoot, naked, uncircumcised. A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: And the women, may my father and mother ransom you? He said: yes. She said: O shame! He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And at what are you amazed, O daughter of Abu Bakr? She said: I am amazed at your hadith, some of them looking at others. He said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck her shoulder and said: O daughter of Abu Quhafah, people that day will be distracted from looking, with their eyes raised upward for forty years, neither eating nor drinking, staring with their eyes; among them one whom sweat reaches his feet, one whom it reaches his legs, one whom it reaches his belly, and one whom sweat bridles from the long standing. Then Allah will have mercy on the servants thereafter, and will order the near angels to carry His throne from the heavens to a white land on which no blood was shed and no sin done, as though white silver. Then the angels will stand encircling the throne, and that is the first day an eye looked to Allah the Mighty and Majestic. Then He will order a caller to call with a voice heard by the two races, jinn and men: where is so-and-so son of so-and-so? He will rise to that and come out of the standing, and Allah the Exalted will acquaint people with him. Then it will be said: his good deeds come out with him, and Allah the Exalted will acquaint the people of the standing with those good deeds. When he stands before the Lord of the worlds it will be said: where are the owners of wrongs? They will come man by man, and it will be said: did you wrong so-and-so so-and-so? He will say: yes, my Lord. That is the day their tongues, feet and hands testify against them for what they earned. His good deeds will be taken and paid to whom he wronged, on a day with no dirham nor dinar, only taking of good deeds and returning of evil deeds. The owners of wrongs will keep taking from his good deeds until no good deed remains for him. Then those remaining who took nothing will stand and say: what of others, we took...? It will be said to them: do not hasten; taken from their evils and returned upon him, until none wronged with a wrong remains. Allah the Exalted will acquaint all the people of the standing with that. When emptied of his good deeds it will be said: return to your mother Hawiyah; no wrong today; Allah is swift in reckoning. No angel, sent prophet, truthful one, martyr nor human will remain that day but will think, from what he sees of severe punishment, that he will not be saved, except whom Allah the Mighty and Majestic protects."
"5457","4555 - Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma' bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah gathers the first and the last on the Day of Resurrection, a caller will come calling with a voice all creatures hear: the people of the gathering will know today who is most worthy of honor. Then he will return and call: let those stand whose sides forsook their beds, the verse. They will stand, few. Then he will return and call: where are those whom neither trade nor sale diverts from the remembrance of Allah, the verse. They will stand, few. Then he will return and call: let those stand who used to praise in ease and hardship. They will stand, few. Then the rest of the people will be reckoned."
"5458","4556 - Zuhayr narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us: Darraj Abu al-Samh narrated to us that Abu al-Haytham told him, from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The earth eats everything of man except the tailbone. It was said: and what is it like, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: like a mustard seed; from it they will grow. Ibn Hibban brought it by way of Ibn Wahb, from Amr ibn al-Harith, saying: Darraj told him with it; and we heard it in elevated form in the Resurrection treatise of Ibn Abi Dawud."
"5459","4557 - Al-Harith said: Hawdhah narrated to us: Awf narrated to us, from Abu al-Minhal, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: When the Day of Resurrection comes the earth will be spread like the spreading of leather in its expanse, so-and-so, with all creatures on a single plain, their jinn and men. When that is, this lowest heaven will be folded away from its people and they will be scattered on the face of the earth; the people of heaven alone will be more than all the people of the earth, their jinn and men, by double. When they are scattered on the face of the earth, the people of the earth will panic toward them and say: is our Lord among you? They will panic at their saying, saying: glory be to our Lord, He is not among us, and He is coming. Then the people of the second heaven will be seized; the people of the second heaven alone will be more than the people of the lowest heaven and all the people of the earth by double. When they are scattered upon the people of the face of the earth, the people of the earth will panic toward them and say: is our Lord among you? They will panic at their saying and say: glory be to our Lord, He is not among us, and He is coming. Then all the heavens will be folded, each heaven doubled over the heaven beneath it and all the people of the earth; each time they are scattered on the face of the earth, the people of the earth will panic toward them and say to them the like of that, and they will return to them the like of that. Then the people of the seventh heaven will be folded; the people of the seventh heaven will be more in people than the six heavens and all the people of the earth by double. Allah Blessed and Exalted will come among them, with the nations kneeling in rows. A caller will call: you will know today who are the companions of honor. Let the praisers of their Lord in every state stand. They will hasten to Paradise. Then he will call a second: they will know today who are the companions of honor. Let those stand whose sides forsook their beds, the verse. They will stand and hasten to Paradise. Then he will call a third: let those stand: Men whom neither trade nor sale diverts from the remembrance of Allah, the verse. They will stand and hasten to Paradise. When He has taken of these three, a neck will come out of the Fire, overlooking the creatures, with two seeing eyes and an eloquent tongue, saying: I am entrusted with every arrogant tyrant, and with whoever set up with Allah another god, and with the picture-makers. It will snatch them like a bird snatches sesame seeds, and cast them into Hell."
"5460","4558 - Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, saying: Abu Asim al-Habati, who was of the best of the people of Basra and of the companions of Haram and Salim ibn Abi Muti', said: Bakr ibn Khunays narrated to us, from Dirar ibn Amr, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas, from Tamim al-Dari (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah Blessed and Exalted will say to the Angel of Death: go to My friend and bring him to Me, for I have tried him in ease and hardship and found him as I love; bring him to Me and I shall rest him. He said: the Angel of Death will go to him with five hundred angels, with shrouds and embalming from Paradise, and with bundles of basil, one basil root with twenty colors on its head, each color with a scent other than its companion's scent; with them white silk with pungent musk. He said: the Angel of Death will sit at his head, the angels surrounding him, each of them placing his hand on a limb of his, with that white silk and pungent musk spread from under his chin; a gate to Paradise will be opened for him, and his soul will be distracted thereat with the fringes of Paradise, at times with its spouses, at times with its clothing, at times with its fruits, as a family distracts a boy when he weeps; his spouses will eagerly hasten to him thereat. The soul will protrude, al-Bursani said: meaning it hastens to come out from what it sees of what it loves. He said: the Angel of Death will say: come out, O good soul, to a lote-tree stripped of thorns, clustered acacia, outspread shade and poured water. He said: the Angel of Death is gentler with him than a mother with her child, knowing that soul is beloved to its Lord, seeking gentleness endearing himself to his Lord and pleasing the Lord with him. His soul will be drawn as a hair is drawn from dough. He said: And Allah the Exalted said: Those whom the angels take good; and He the Mighty and Majestic said: If he is of the brought near, then rest. The hadith in full is long; and as for the wicked soul its drawing is like drawing a many-branched skewer from wet wool."
"5461","4559 - Abu Ya'la said: Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us: Yunus, that is Ibn Bukayr, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn al-Mughirah, from Sulayman ibn Amr al-Utwar who was an orphan of Abu Sa'id, from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah the Exalted gathers people on a single plain on the Day of Resurrection, the Fire will come riding upon itself, its keepers restraining it, saying: by my Lord's might, you shall leave between me and my spouses or I shall overwhelm people with a single neck. They will say: who are your spouses? It will say: every arrogant tyrant. It will put out its tongue and snatch them with it from among people and cast them into it. Then it will withdraw, then come riding upon itself, its keepers restraining it, saying: by my Lord's might, you shall leave between me and my spouses or I shall overwhelm people with a single neck. They will say: who are your spouses? It will say: every conceited boaster. It will snatch them with its tongue and cast them into its belly. Then it will withdraw, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic will judge between the servants."
"5462","4560 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, saying: he heard Ubayd ibn Umayr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted will bring out people from the Fire after they were scorched in it and became charcoal; they will be cast into a river at the gate of Paradise called the River of Life, and will grow in it as grain grows in flood-borne soil, or as hair tufts grow; they will enter Paradise and it will be said: these are Allah the Mighty and Majestic's freed ones from the Fire. A man accused of Kharijite views, called Harun Abu Musa, or Abu Musa ibn Harun, said: what is this you tell Abu Asim? He said: away from me, O barbarian; had I not heard it from more than thirty of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I would not have told it. Sound; al-Bukhari brought it from the narration of Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"5463","Chapter 46: Intercession, with hadiths of the resurrection. 4561 - Abu Bakr said: Shabbabah ibn Sawwar narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: People foul-smelling, scorched by the Fire, will come out of the Fire and enter Paradise by the intercession of the intercessors, named therein the Hell-dwellers. Good, sound."
"5464","4562 - Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn Jammaz narrated to us, from Abu Dawud, who had met a dozen of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from Zayd ibn Arqam and others of the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intercession on the Day of Resurrection is true; whoever does not believe in it will not be of its people."
"5465","4563 - Al-Harith said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Ya'qub narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Shaghaf, from Abdullah ibn Salam (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The most honored of Allah the Exalted's creation to Him is Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Paradise is in heaven and Hell in earth. When the Day of Resurrection comes Allah will raise creation nation by nation and prophet by prophet, until Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the last of creation in station. Then a bridge will be laid over Hell, then it will be called: where is Muhammad and his ummah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will stand, followed by his ummah, righteous and wicked."
"5466","4564 - Abu Ya'la said: Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us: Yunus, that is Ibn Bukayr, narrated to us: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will make Himself known to me on the Day of Resurrection, and I shall prostrate a prostration with which He is pleased with me; then I shall praise Him with praise with which He is pleased with me; then I shall be permitted to speak. Then my ummah will pass over the Path laid across the midst of Hell; they will pass swifter than a glance and an arrow, then swifter than the best horses, until a man comes out of it crawling; they are the deeds; Hell will ask for more until He places His foot in it, and part of it will shrink to part, saying: enough, enough; and I shall be at the Pool. It was said: what is the Pool, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, its drink is whiter than milk, sweeter than honey, colder than snow, more fragrant than musk; its vessels more than the number of stars; no man drinks from it then thirsts ever, nor is turned away then quenched ever."
"5467","4565 - Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Salih: Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from Abu al-Za'ra', from Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People of the Muslims scorched in the Fire will enter Paradise, by Allah the Exalted's mercy and the intercession of the intercessors."
"5468","4566/1 - Abu Bakr and al-Harith both said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Anas, from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have seen what my ummah will meet after me, so I have delayed my intercession to the Day of Resurrection."
"5469","4566/2 - Abu Ya'la said: Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us: Musa ibn Ubaydah al-Rabadhi narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyash al-Zuraqi, from Anas, from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with them both), with it."
"5470","4566/3 - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, and he mentioned similar to it."
"5471","4567 - Al-Harith said: Ishaq ibn Bishr narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Salim narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar told me, from Abu Bakr ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall be raised on the Day of Resurrection between Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both); then I shall go to the people of Baqi' al-Gharqad, and they will be raised with me; then I shall await the people of Makkah until they come to me, and I shall be raised between the people of the two sanctuaries."
"5472","4568 - Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us: Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Ibn al-Munkadir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall hear the Cry and go out to al-Baqi', and be gathered with them."
"5473","4569 - Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Hazim narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Mujahid, who said: The heaven will rain until the earth splits over the dead, and they will come out."
"5474","4570 - Dawud narrated to us: Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Zayd, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A son of Adam will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and stood between the two scales of the Balance, with an angel put in charge of him; if his scale is heavy the angel will call with a voice all creatures hear: so-and-so has prospered with a prosperity after which he will never be wretched; if his scale is light the angel will call with a voice all creatures hear: so-and-so is wretched with a wretchedness after which he will never prosper. Al-Bazzar narrated it, from Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith, from Dawud, saying: we know it narrated from Thabit only by Salih, nor from Ja'far except by Salih."
"5475","4571/1 - Al-Harith said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us: Bashir ibn al-Muhajir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you but his Lord of the worlds will question him, with no veil nor interpreter between Him and him."
"5476","4571/2 - Al-Bazzar narrated it, from Safwan al-Muflis, from Abd al-Aziz, pointing to his solitariness with it."
"5477","4572 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah: Abu Ishaq narrated to me, from Silah, from Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: People will be gathered on a single plain, and the caller will make them hear and sight will reach them; the first called will be Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he will say: at Your service and blessedness; good is in Your hands, and evil is not to You; guided is whom You guide; Your servant before You; I am from You and to You; no refuge nor escape from You except to You; blessed and exalted are You; glory be to You, Lord of the House. That is His the Mighty and Majestic's saying: It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praised station."
"5478","4573/1 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Abdullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us: Ma'mar told us, from Abu Ishaq, from Silah ibn Zufar, from Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Allah the Exalted will gather people on the Day of Resurrection on a single plain, barefoot, naked, as they were first created; the caller will make them hear and sight will reach them; and he mentioned similar to it."
"5479","4573/2 - Al-Harith said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, and he mentioned the like of Shu'bah's hadith."
"5480","4573/3 - Abu Ya'la said: Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, with it."
"5481","4573/4 - Al-Bazzar said: Muhammad narrated to us: Muhammad narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, with it. Al-Hakim declared it sound."
"5482","4574/1 - Abu Bakr said: Ahmad ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abu Khalid Yazid al-Asadi narrated to us: Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Alqamah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Aqil al-Thaqafi, who said: I went in the delegation of Thaqif; we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), staying at the door, with no man among people more hateful to us than the man we would enter upon; and we left with no man among people dearer to us than the man we entered upon. One of us said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not ask your Lord for a kingdom like the kingdom of Sulayman son of Dawud? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled, then said: Perhaps for your companion with Allah the Exalted is better than the kingdom of Sulayman; Allah the Exalted sent no prophet but gave him a supplication: some took with it a world and were given it, some called with it upon their people when they disobeyed him and they perished by it; Allah the Mighty and Majestic has given me a supplication, and I have hidden it as intercession with my Lord for my ummah on the Day of Resurrection."
"5483","4574/2 - Al-Harith said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban told us: Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Abbas al-Shibami narrated to us: Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah narrated to us, similar to it."
"5484","4574/3 - Abu Ya'la said: Zuhayr narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Yunus narrated to us, and he mentioned it."
"5485","4574/4 - Al-Bazzar said: al-Abbas ibn Abi Talib narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, and he mentioned it. And he said: we know for Ibn Abi Aqil only this."
"5486","4575 - Abu Bakr said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Uthman, from Salman (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: They will come to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and say to him: O Prophet of Allah, you are the one by whom Allah opened and sealed, and forgave you what preceded of your sin and what followed; you have come this day secure, and you see what we are in; stand and intercede for us to our Lord. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will say: I am your man. He will go out and gather people until he reaches the gate of Paradise, take a golden ring on the gate and knock the gate. It will be said: who is this? It will be said: Muhammad. It will be opened for him until he stands before Allah the Mighty and Majestic; he will ask leave to prostrate and be permitted; he will be called: O Muhammad, raise your head, ask and be given, intercede and be heard, call and be answered. He said: a gate of praise of Him, lauding and glorifying, will be opened for him such as was opened to none of creation. He will be called: O Muhammad, raise your head, ask and be given, intercede and be heard, call and be answered. He will raise his head and say: my Lord, my ummah, my ummah, two or three times. Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: he will intercede for everyone in whose heart is a wheat grain's weight of faith, or a barley grain's weight of faith, or a mustard seed's weight of faith. That is the praised station. Sound, stopped."
"5487","4576 - Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Shuja' al-Balkhi narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn Jammaz narrated to us, from al-Raqashi, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall keep interceding for my ummah until it is said: O Muhammad, bring out of the Fire whoever has in his heart the weight of a barley grain, until he said: it will be said: O Muhammad, bring out whoever has in his heart the measure of a gnat's wing of faith."
"5488","4577 - Abu Ya'la said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Abu Shihab narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, who said: Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall knock the gate of Paradise; a gate of gold will be opened with a ring of silver; the greatest light will meet me and I shall fall prostrate; there will be cast upon me of praise of Allah the Mighty and Majestic what was cast upon none before me. It will be said: raise your head, ask and be given, speak and be heard, intercede and be heard. I shall say: my ummah. It will be said: for you whoever has in his heart the weight of a barley grain, until he said: a mustard seed, until he said: whoever said: there is no god but Allah."
"5489","4578 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Warkani narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn: a man of knowledge narrated to me, saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earth will be spread like leather for Allah the Mighty and Majestic's greatness, and no man of the sons of Adam will have in it but his feet's place. Then I shall be called first of people and fall prostrate; then I shall be permitted and say: my Lord, this one told me, and Jibril (peace be upon him) is at the right of the Throne, by Allah he never saw him before it, that You sent him to me; and Jibril is silent, not speaking. Allah the Mighty and Majestic will say: he spoke true. Then I shall be permitted intercession, and I shall say: my Lord, Your servants worshipped You in the ends of the earth. That is the praised station. Al-Hakim declared it sound."
"5490","Chapter 47: The first to be clothed on the Day of Resurrection. 4579/1 - Ishaq said: Ubayd ibn Sa'id al-Umawi told us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The first to be clothed on the Day of Resurrection is Ibrahim (peace and prayer be upon him), with two Coptic garments, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he is at the right of the Throne."
"5491","4579/2 - Abu Ya'la said: Ubaydullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, with this. It is in a long hadith from the Musnad of Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him); Ahmad brought it."
"5492","Chapter 48: Wrongs. 4580 - Abd said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us: Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us: Abu Harun narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No believer wrongs a believer but Allah will avenge him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5493","4581 - Abu Dawud said: al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Yazid, that is al-Raqashi, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wrongdoing is three: a wrong Allah the Exalted will not leave, a wrong forgiven, and a wrong not forgiven. As for the wrong not forgiven, it is associating partners, which Allah does not forgive. As for the wrong forgiven, it is a servant's wrong between him and his Lord the Mighty and Majestic. As for what is left, Allah the Mighty and Majestic will settle some of them from others."
"5494","4582 - Musaddad said: Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Uthman, who said: A man will come on the Day of Resurrection with good deeds like firm mountains; a man will keep seeking him for a wrong and taking from his good deeds until no good deed of his remains, and until there returns to him of their evils. I said to Abu Uthman: from whom did you hear this? He mentioned six of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I remembered of them Ibn Mas'ud, Hudhayfah and Salman (may Allah be pleased with them)."
"5495","Chapter 49: Intercession of the believers. 4583 - Abu Ya'la said: al-Salt ibn Mas'ud narrated to us: Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Abu Zilal narrated to me: Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Two men crossed a desert, one a worshipper and the other given to levity; the worshipper thirsted until he fell; his companion kept looking at him fallen and said: by Allah, if this righteous servant dies of thirst while I have water, I shall gain no good from Allah; if I give him my water I shall die. He relied on Allah the Exalted, resolved, sprinkled him with some of his water and gave him to drink of his surplus; he rose, and they crossed the desert. He said: the one given to levity will be stopped on the Day of Resurrection for reckoning and ordered to the Fire; the angels will drive him, and he will see the worshipper and say: O so-and-so, do you not know me? He will say: who are you? He will say: I am so-and-so who preferred you over myself on the desert day. He said: he will say: yes, I know you. He will say to the angels: stop. He will be stopped, and he will come and stand and call his Lord, saying: my Lord, You know his hand with me, how he preferred me over himself; my Lord, grant him to me. He, majestic and lofty, will say: he is yours. He said: he will come and take his hand and enter him into Paradise. Ja'far said: I said to him: did Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) tell you? He said: yes."
"5496","4584/1 - Musaddad said: Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rows of the people of the Fire will come out; a man will pass by a man of the people of Paradise and say: O so-and-so, do you not know me? He will say: who are you? He will say: I am the one from whom you asked water for ablution and I gave you. He will intercede for him and be heard for him. A man will pass by a man and say: O so-and-so, do you not know me? He will say: who are you? He will say: did you not send me on such-and-such a need and I fulfilled it for you? He will intercede for him and be heard for him. In it is al-Raqashi, who is weak."
"5497","4584/2 - Abu Ya'la said: al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, with it. Yusuf is abandoned in hadith."
"5498","4585 - Rawh ibn Abd al-Mu'min narrated to us: Ali ibn Abi Sarah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man of the people of Paradise will look upon a man of the people of the Fire; one in the Fire will call: O so-and-so, do you not know me? He will say: no, by Allah, I do not know you; who are you, woe to you? He will say: I am the one you passed by in this world and asked me for a drink of water and I gave you; intercede for me with it to your Lord. He said: that man will enter upon Allah in his visit and say: my Lord, I looked upon the people of the Fire, and a man of the people of the Fire stood and called: O so-and-so, do you not know me? I said: by Allah, I do not know you; who are you? He said: I am the one you passed by in this world and asked me and I gave you; intercede for me with it to your Lord. He will say: my Lord, let me intercede for him. He said: Allah will let him intercede for him and bring him out of the Fire."
"5499","4586 - Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us: Rawh ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us: Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), and he mentioned it, adding: And the confirmation of this in the Qur'an: If you avoid the major sins you are forbidden, We shall expiate your evils and admit you to a noble entrance, the verse. These are those who avoid major sins, and these are those who fall into them; the intercession of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is established for them."
"5500","4587 - Musaddad said: Isma'il narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: More than Banu Tamim will enter Paradise by the intercession of a man of my ummah."
"5501","4588 - Abu Ya'la said: Khalaf narrated to us: Abu al-Mutarrif al-Mughirah al-Shami narrated to us, from al-Arzami, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah gathers creation on the Day of Resurrection, a caller will call: where are the people of merit? Few people will stand and hasten to Paradise swiftly. The angels will meet them and say: we see you hastening to Paradise; who are you? They will say: we are the people of merit. They will say: what is your merit? They will say: when we were wronged we were patient, when evil was done to us we pardoned, when ignorance was shown to us we were forbearing. It will be said to them: enter Paradise; excellent is the reward of the workers. Then a caller will call: where are the patient? Few people will come forth and hasten to Paradise swiftly. He said: the angels will meet them and say: we see you hastening to Paradise; who are you? They will say: we are the patient. They will say: what is your patience? They will say: we were patient in obeying Allah the Exalted, and patient against disobeying Allah the Mighty and Majestic. It will be said to them: enter Paradise; excellent is the reward of the workers. Then a caller will call: where are those who loved one another for Allah the Exalted, or he said: for Allah's sake the Mighty and Majestic, Abu Muhammad doubting. Few people will stand and hasten to Paradise swiftly. The angels will meet them and say: we see you hastening to Paradise; who are you? They will say: we are those who loved one another for Allah the Mighty and Majestic, or for Allah's sake the Mighty and Majestic. They will say: what was your deed? They will say: we loved one another for Allah the Mighty and Majestic and visited one another for Allah. It will be said to them: enter Paradise; excellent is the reward of the workers."
"5502","Chapter 50: Knowledge of the first with which Allah the Exalted addresses the believers. 4589 - Abu Dawud said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from Abu Ayyash, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish I shall tell you of the first that Allah the Mighty and Majestic will say to the believers on the Day of Resurrection, and of the first they will say. They said: yes, O Messenger of Allah. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Blessed and Exalted will say to the believers on the Day of Resurrection: did you love meeting Me? They will say: yes, our Lord. He will say: why? They will say: we hoped for Your pardon and forgiveness. He will say: I have made My mercy due for you."
"5503","Chapter 51: Pardoning wrongs. 4590 - Abu Ya'la said: Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abbad ibn Shaybah al-Habati narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Anas, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting, we saw him laugh until his front teeth showed. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: what made you laugh, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother ransom you? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two kneeling men of my ummah before the Lord of Might, majestic in majesty; one of them said: my Lord, take for me my wrong from my brother. Allah the Mighty and Majestic said: give your brother his wrong. He said: my Lord, nothing of my good deeds remains. He said: my Lord, let him bear of my burdens. He said: the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) overflowed with weeping. Then he said: that is a mighty day; people will need therein to have their burdens borne from them. Allah Blessed and Exalted will say to the seeker: raise your sight and look into the Gardens. He will raise his head and say: my Lord, I see cities of silver and palaces of gold crowned with pearls; for which prophet is this? For which truthful one? For which martyr? He will say: this is for whoever gives the price. He will say: my Lord, who owns that? He, majestic and lofty, will say: you own it. He will say: with what, my Lord? He will say: by pardoning your brother. He will say: my Lord, I have pardoned him. Allah the Exalted will say: take your brother's hand and enter him into Paradise. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said of that: So fear Allah and amend your relations."
"5504","4591 - Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us: Kawthar ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: We were told that when the Day of Resurrection comes a caller will call: where are the pardoners? He said: Allah the Exalted will recompense them for their pardoning people."
"5505","4592/1 - Abu Ya'la said: Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Sadhus, keeper of al-Sabiri, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When creation meet on the Day of Resurrection, and the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire the Fire, a caller heard by creation will call: O people of the gathering, forgo wrongs among you, and your reward is upon Me."
"5506","4592/2 - Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Sinan narrated to us, similar to it."
"5507","Chapter 52: Description of the Fire and its people, may Allah save us from it. 4593 - Abu Bakr said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Sa'ib ibn Malik, from Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I entered Paradise and saw most of its people the poor; I looked into the Fire and saw most of its people the rich and women; I saw in it three punished: a tall Himyari woman who tied a cat of hers, neither feeding nor watering it, nor leaving it to eat of the earth's vermin, so it mauls her front and back; I saw therein the brother of Banu Da'da' who used to steal from pilgrims with his hooked staff, and when noticed said: it only caught on my staff; and the one who stole the two sacrificial camels of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This is a hasan chain."
"5508","4594/1 - Abu Bakr said: I was told, from Jarir, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had a stone been cast from the edge of Hell it would fall seventy autumns before settling in its bottom."
"5509","4594/2 - Abu Ya'la said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us."
"5510","4594/3 - Al-Bazzar said: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, both saying: Jarir narrated to us. Ibn Hibban declared it sound from Jarir's hadith, with it."
"5511","4595/1 - Abu Ya'la said: Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us: Abu Ubaydah narrated to us: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Shabib, from Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyyah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Were there in this mosque a hundred thousand or more, with among them a man of the people of the Fire, and he breathed and his breath touched them, the mosque with all in it would burn. Al-Bazzar narrated it by this way, and its men are trustworthy."
"5512","4596 - Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Mu'ayqib, from Sulayman ibn Amr al-Utwar who was an orphan in the care of Abu Sa'id, from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah gathers people on a single plain on the Day of Resurrection, the Fire will come riding upon itself, its keepers restraining it, the hadith. It has preceded in the resurrection chapter."
"5513","4597 - Abu Bakr said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day heard a din and said: O Jibril, what is this? He said: a stone cast from the edge of Hell seventy autumns ago; now it has settled in its bottom."
"5514","4598 - Abu Ya'la said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were a stone like seven pregnant camels with their fat and offspring cast into Hell, it would fall seventy years without reaching its bottom."
"5515","4599 - Abu Bakr said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Harun ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, who said: I heard Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) say: We were one day with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw him gloomy. Some of us said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother ransom you, why do we see you gloomy? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I heard a thud the like of which I never heard; Jibril (peace be upon him) came to me and I asked him about it, and he said: this is a rock cast into the Fire seventy autumns ago; today it reached its resting place. Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) said: By the One who took the soul of Muhammad our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we never saw him laugh after that day until we buried him in dust."
"5516","4600 - Abu Ya'la said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Muslim Abu Sa'id narrated to us: Ziyad al-Numayri narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Fire complained to its Lord the Mighty and Majestic, saying: my Lord, part of me eats part; He made for it two breaths: a breath in winter and a breath in summer; the severity of heat you find is of its heat, and the severity of cold you find is of its frost."
"5517","4601 - Abdullah ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Imran ibn Zayd: Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O people! Weep, and if you do not weep then force weeping, for the people of the Fire will weep in the Fire until their tears flow on their cheeks as though streams, until tears cease, then blood will flow, wounding the eye."
"5518","Chapter 53: Description of Paradise and its people. 4601/1 - Ishaq said: Abd al-Razzaq told us: al-Thawri and Ma'mar narrated to us, each adding over his companion, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), concerning His the Exalted's saying: And those who feared their Lord will be driven to Paradise in troops, until when they come to it: they will find at the gate of Paradise a tree from whose trunk, Ma'mar said, from whose root, al-Thawri said, two springs come out; they will go to one of them, as though ordered to it, Ma'mar said: and wash with it, al-Thawri said: and perform ablution from it; their heads will never be disheveled thereafter, nor their skins changed thereafter, as though oiled with oil; the bloom of bliss will run upon them. Then they will go to the other and drink from it, and it will purify their bellies; no filth, harm nor evil will remain in their bellies but will come out. The angels will meet them at the gate of Paradise: Peace be upon you, you were good, so enter it abiding. The youths will meet them like hidden pearls, like scattered pearls, telling them of what Allah the Exalted prepared for them, circling them as the youths of this world circle a beloved returning from absence, saying: rejoice, Allah has prepared for you so-and-so, and prepared for you so-and-so. Then a boy of them will go to a wife of his wives and say: so-and-so has come, by the name he was called by in this world. Joy will lighten her till she stands on her door's threshold..."
"5519","4601/2 - Yahya ibn Adam told us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: he mentioned the Fire and magnified its affair, then said: Those who feared their Lord will be driven to Paradise in troops, and he mentioned similar to it, saying: Then pearl-built mansions above them, a red, green and yellow palace. He said: Then they will look at that bliss, recline upon it and say: Praise be to Allah who guided us to this."
"5520","4601/3 - Yahya told us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, with this chain, similar to it, saying: Then he will recline on a couch of his couches, then say: praise be to Allah."
"5521","4601/4 - Yahya said: Hamzah al-Zayyat narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: he mentioned the Fire, mentioning of it what Allah willed him to mention, then said: In extended columns. Then he said: And those who feared their Lord will be driven to Paradise in troops, and he mentioned similar to Zuhayr's hadith. This is a sound hadith, with the ruling of raised, since there is no room for opinion in such matters. 4601/5 - Al-Baghawi narrated it in al-Ja'diyyat from Ali ibn al-Ja'd, from Zuhayr, in full. 4601/6 - Abu Nu'aym narrated it in the Description of Paradise from Ibn Faris, from Muhammad ibn Asim, from Abu Yahya al-Himmani, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, in full."
"5522","4602 - Abd and al-Harith said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us: Husayn ibn Umar narrated to us: Mukhariq narrated to us, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: People of the Jews came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, is there fruit in Paradise? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, in it are fruit, palms and pomegranates. They said: will they eat as they eat in this world? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: yes, and multiples of that. They said: will they relieve themselves? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: no, but they will sweat then perspire, and Allah the Exalted will remove what harm is in their bellies."
"5523","4603/1 - Ibn Abi Umar said: al-Muqri' narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um al-Ifriqi narrated to us: Umarah ibn Rashid ibn Muslim al-Kinani, of the people of Damascus, narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked: will the people of Paradise touch their wives? He said: Yes, with a member that does not tire, a part that does not wear, and desire that does not cease."
"5524","4603/2 - Al-Bazzar said: Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: al-Muqri' narrated to us, with it."
"5525","4604 - Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Hilal al-Khawlani narrated to us, from Safwan, from al-Haytham al-Ta'i and Sulaym ibn Amir, both saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about intercourse in Paradise, and he said: Yes, a delightful midday rest, with a member that does not tire; a man will recline therein the reclining for forty years, not moving from it nor tiring of it; there will come to him therein what his soul desires and his eye delights in."
"5526","4605 - Abu Ya'la said: Suwayd narrated to us: Khalid ibn Abi Malik narrated to us, from his father, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: will the people of Paradise have intercourse? He said: Yes, vigorously, but no semen nor death."
"5527","4606 - Abu Hammam narrated to us: Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi al-Hawari, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we go to our women in Paradise as we go to them in this world? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose hand is Muhammad's soul, a man will go in a single morning to a hundred virgins."
"5528","4607 - Abu al-Harith Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Mujalid narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: will we weave our clothes in Paradise with our hands? The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed. The bedouin said: why do you laugh at an ignorant one asking a learned one? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You spoke true, O bedouin, but they are fruits."
"5529","4608 - Surayj narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from Musa ibn Qays, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Sa'id ibn Amir ibn Hidhyam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were a woman of the wide-eyed houris to bring out her hand, every souled being would find its scent; shall I leave them for you? More fitting that I leave you to them."
"5530","4609 - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Umar narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Fulan ibn Abdullah ibn Rafi', from one of the children of Anas ibn Malik, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wide-eyed houris will sing in Paradise, saying..."
"5531","4610 - Musaddad said: Mu'tamir narrated to us, saying: I heard my father say: I heard Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The people of Paradise will say: come with us to the market. They will go to pulpits of mounds of musk, or mountains of musk. When they return to their wives, their wives will say: we find from you a scent we did not find when you left us; and they will say: we find from you a scent we did not find when we left you, or as he said."
"5532","4611 - Abu Bakr said: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us: Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, from Umar ibn Rabi'ah, from al-Hasan, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: how is Paradise? He said: Whoever enters Paradise lives and does not die, enjoys until he knows no misery; his clothes do not wear out, his youth does not perish. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how is its building? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A brick of silver and a brick of gold; its mortar pungent musk; its pebbles pearls and rubies; its soil saffron."
"5533","4612 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan and Shu'bah, from Sulayman, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, who said: Gardens of Eden are the belly of Paradise. I said: what is the belly of Paradise? Sulayman said: its middle."
"5534","4613/1 - Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there are columns of ruby, upon them chambers of chrysolite, with opened doors shining as the brilliant star shines. It was said: who dwells them, O Prophet of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: those who love one another for Allah, sit together for Allah, and spend for one another for Allah."
"5535","4613/2 - Abd said: Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, with it. Weak."
"5536","4614 - Al-Harith said: Sa'id ibn Shurahbil narrated to us, from al-Layth, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, who said: Ka'b said: The Nile river is the river of honey in Paradise, the Tigris river the river of milk in Paradise, the Euphrates river the river of wine in Paradise, and the Sayhan river the river of water in Paradise. He said: Allah the Exalted extinguished their light to place them in Paradise."
"5537","4616 - Abu Ya'la said: Uqbah narrated to us: Yunus told us: Ibn Ishaq told us, from Ubaydullah ibn al-Mughirah, from Sulayman ibn Amr, from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise was shown to me, and I went to take a bunch from it to show you, but was kept from it. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, like the grapes of Paradise? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Like the greatest bucket your mother ever emptied."
"5538","4616/1 - Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad ibn Hatim narrated to us: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Humayd al-A'raj, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will look at a bird in Paradise and desire it, and it will fall before you roasted."
"5539","4616/2 - Al-Bazzar said: al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us: Khalaf narrated to us with this, saying: we know it only by this way, and Humayd is Ibn Ata', a Kufi, weak. I said: we heard it elevated in the part of al-Hasan ibn Arafah."
"5540","4617 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Abu Zibyan, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: Nothing in this world of what is in Paradise but names."
"5541","4618 - Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn al-Munkadir, who said: I heard Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) say: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise, Allah the Mighty and Majestic will say: shall I give you better than this? They will say: our Lord, what is better than this? He, Blessed and Exalted, will say: My pleasure."
"5542","4619 - Abd said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us: Abu Shihab narrated to us: Khalid ibn Dinar al-Nili told me, from Hammad ibn Ja'far, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: Shall I tell you of the lowest of the people of Paradise? They said: yes. He said: A man will enter from the gate of Paradise, and his youths will meet him, saying: welcome, our master, it is time for you to return. He said: Carpets will be spread for him for forty years. Then he will look right and left and see the gardens, saying: whose is what is here? It will be said: yours. When he finishes, a red ruby or green emerald will be raised for him, with seventy branches, in each branch seventy rooms, in each room seventy doors. It will be said to him: recite and ascend. He said: he will ascend until when he reaches the throne of his kingship he will recline upon it, a mile by a mile, with surplus about him; seventy thousand plates of gold will be brought to him, no plate of its companion's color; he will find the savor of the last as he finds the savor of the first. Then drinks of colors will be brought to him, and he will drink of them what he desires. Then the youths will say: leave him and his wives. Abu Shihab said: I think he said: the youths will withdraw from him, and behold a houri sitting on the throne of her kingship; he will see the marrow of her leg from behind flesh and blood, and say to her: who are you? She will say: I am of the wide-eyed houris kept for you. He will look at her forty years without raising his sight from her. Then he will raise his sight to the rooms above him, and behold another handsomer than her. She will say to him: Has not..."
"5543","4620 - Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri' in the additions of the Musnad of Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Amr ibn Khalid al-Wasiti: Zayd ibn Ali narrated to us, from his fathers, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Day of Resurrection comes Allah the Exalted will separate the people of Paradise from the people of the Fire; and on Monday and Thursday pulpits of light will be placed around the Throne, and pulpits of chrysolite and ruby. The angels entrusted with them will say: Lord, for whom did You place these pulpits? It will be cast on their mouths: for the strangers. They will say: Lord, who are the strangers? It will be cast on their mouths: people who loved one another for Allah the Mighty and Majestic without seeing Him. While so, each man of them will come, more knowing of his seat than one of you of his seat in his dome with his wife in the house of this world; their nearness to the Lord Blessed and Exalted according to their ranks in Paradise. When the people are complete, the Lord the Mighty and Majestic will say: My servants, My creation, My visitors, those loving one another in My majesty without seeing Me, feed them. They will feed them. Then He will say: delight them. Then fruit will be brought with every desire, delight and sweet scent. Then the Lord will say: give them drink. Vessels will be brought, none knowing whether the vessel is whiter or what is in it. Then He will say: clothe them. Fruits splitting the earth like the breasts of virgins among women will be brought, in each fruit seventy robes..."
"5544","Chapter 54. 4621 - Abu Bakr said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Atik narrated to us, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: I came to visit the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), and revelation was coming to him; when it was lifted from him, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to A'ishah: hand me my cloak. He went out and entered the mosque, in which were people, no others in the mosque; he sat in a side of the people, until when the reminder finished his reminding he recited the Tanzeel of prostration, and people were unable for the mosque. A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) sent to her family: attend the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for I have seen from him what I never saw. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head, and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: you prolonged the prostration, O Messenger of Allah. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I prostrated in thanks to my Lord for what He gave me of my ummah: seventy thousand entering Paradise. Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah, your ummah is more and better, ask increase for them, until he said two or three times. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: may my father ransom you, O Messenger of Allah, your ummah has encompassed you."
"5545","4622 - Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Isa narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Layla, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: Seventy thousand of my ummah will enter Paradise with no reckoning upon them. Ukkashah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Prophet of Allah, call upon Allah the Exalted to make me of them. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make him of them. Another man said: call upon Allah the Exalted to make me of them. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make him of them. Then the people were silent a while and spoke. Some said: had we said: O Messenger of Allah, call upon Allah to make us of them. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ukkashah and his companion preceded you; had you said, I would have said, and had I said it would have been due."
"5546","4623 - Abu Ya'la said: al-Muqaddami narrated to us: Abd al-Qahir ibn al-Sari narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Seventy thousand of my ummah will enter Paradise. They said: increase us, O Messenger of Allah. He said: for each man seventy thousand. They said: increase us, O Messenger of Allah. He was on a mound and scooped with his hand. They said: increase us, O Messenger of Allah. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: this, scooping with his hands. They said: O Prophet of Allah, may Allah distance whoever enters the Fire after this."
"5547","4624 - Umayyah ibn Bistam told us: Mu'tamir narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Hammad, from Unaysah bint Zayd ibn Arqam, from her father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Zayd in an illness of his, saying: There is no harm to you from this illness of yours, but how will you be when you live long after me and go blind? He said: then I shall reckon and be patient. He said: then you will enter Paradise without reckoning. He said: he went blind after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, then Allah returned his sight to him, then he died."
"5548","4625 - Zuhayr narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Darraj, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Zuhayr doubting: Whoever of the people of this world dies, young or old, will be returned to sixty years, never exceeding it, in Paradise; and likewise the people of the Fire."
"5549","4626 - Abu Ya'la said: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Sinan: Abu Yahya al-Kala'i narrated to us, saying: I came to al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib in the mosque and said: O Abu Yazid, people claim you did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: glory be to Allah; by Allah, I saw him while I walked with my uncle; he took this ear of mine and said to my uncle: do you think this one remembers his mother or father? We said to him: tell us something you heard from him. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The miscarried fetus to the aged elder will be gathered as sons of thirty-three, in the creation of Adam, the beauty of Yusuf, and the heart of Ayyub, hairless, kohled. I said: how of the disbeliever? He said: he will be magnified for the Fire until his skin becomes forty cubits, and every molar of his molars like Uhud."
"5550","Chapter 55: The last to enter Paradise. 4627 - Abu Bakr said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, from Awf ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I know the last of the people of Paradise to enter it: a man who used to ask Allah the Exalted to move him away from the Fire, the hadith. Its explanation has preceded in the chapter of the description of the resurrection. I ask Allah the Exalted to move me away from the Fire and enter me into Paradise, by His favor and generosity, amen. The second part is done, completing the whole book al-Matalib al-Aliyah on the additions of the eight Musnads, compiled by the learned imam, shaykh of Islam, seal of memorizers, chief judge Shihab al-Din Abu al-Fadl Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Hajar al-Asqalani al-Misri al-Shafi'i, may Allah enfold him in His mercy and lodge him in the midst of His Paradise, amen. May Allah bless our master Muhammad and his family and grant peace; Allah suffices us, an excellent trustee."
